    "created_at": "2017-01-20T17:03:32Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-01-20T17:03:32Z",
    "body": "3/4 engines don't implement separate processes with direct object references between the processes, as far as I know.\r\n\r\nI do agree that for something like out of process iframes a plan is needed.  It's not quite clear what that plan should be, but yes, it needs to take into account things like indexed access and .parent, and the fact that both of those can go \"out of process\" and then come back \"in-process\" (e.g. as you traverse the .parent chain: you can have page A in process 1 framing page B in process 2, which frames page C which is same-origin with A and hence needs to be back in process 1).\r\n\r\nI agree that this is a problem worth solving, given the desire to do things like out of process iframes.  It's not clear what the right solution is, and I agree with Anne that various other changes to the spec around Location will likely be needed as well...",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
